tudy  researchers use multi-omics data  integration to look at different types  of molecular profiles  integrate them and compare them to  reference databases like the tcga  to understand response to treatment to  drugs that are either already used in  the clinic or being studied in clinical  trials to continue learning we invite  you to explore these associated  resources for the lecture  we will go over the coursework the case  studies and other examples from  literature  to benefit from today's lecture you can  select one of these to refresh your  memory of basic terminology  learn more about the various techniques  or practice what we have learned with  curated data sets on the topics that we  covered in today's session  the contents of the session correspond  with practical lessons that you can  complete independently that are  available on the onyx logic learn portal  with the full course specific lessons  that are of relevance to today's session  include lesson 2 bioinformatics in  healthcare from course 1 introduction to  bioinformatics  in this lesson you will get an overview  of examples from healthcare area where  bioinformatics can be applied you will  also see examples and videos of medical  professionals discussing bioinformatics  and precision medicine applications  another good course to look at is bytes  and molecules  this course is a great place for those  who was confused by a lot of the terms  that we used in today's lecture anyone  that would like to review the basic  terminology and get a good overview of  topics that we cover in this course  should look at this course in full but  specifically we looked at this lesson  lesson six called introduction to  genomics if you are interested in  genomics you can also look at these  additional lessons in the course three  course called genomics in lesson two you  will see how you can work with dna  sequences in r  and in lesson 3 you will get an  introduction to large scale genomics the  full course contains a lot more  information that you can choose to  explore independently some of these will  be covered in the future lectures but do  not worry about completing them for now  at the end you will also find examples  that i already mentioned  these examples include such projects  like ebola  immune response changes in cancer  modeling cancer precision medicine  or tuberculosis infection and treatment  finding drug resistance variants  so let's recap what we have learned so  far  first  we learned how combining clinical and  molecular data helps reveal underlying  factors contributing to the disease  which further helps us provide a precise  diagnosis and effective treatment to the  patient  further we learned about next generation  sequencing technologies for genomic  transcriptomic and metagenomic data that  provide important insights for precision  medicine applications  we also discussed the role of  bioinformatics in taking research  results from the lab to the clinic to  benefit patient treatment and diagnosis  finally we introduced a set of case  studies in precision medicine from  inherited sickle cell anemia to drug  resistance in mycobacterium tuberculosis  in the next session session two on  genomic data analysis we will go one  step further to better understand what  is genomic data  how do you perform variant calling  analysis  what is the difference between germline  and somatic mutations  and how to determine a variance clinical  relevance  at the end of session 2 you will have a  thorough understanding of genomic data  variant calling analysis as well as  specific techniques for clinical  annotation of variants in cancer
 

